bSocket server that hosts AI agents and proxies requests to Claude API. Features:\n    68→- WebSocket-based client communication\n    69→- MCP tool registration and execution\n    70→- Conversation history management\n    71→- Claude API integration\n    72→\n    73→### example\n    74→\n    75→An AI-powered todo list application demonstrating the use-ai library. The AI can:\n    76→- Add, delete, and toggle todos via natural language\n    77→- Query the current todo list\n    78→- Understand context and perform multiple operations\n    79→\n    80→## Tech Stack\n    81→\n    82→- **Runtime**: Bun\n    83→- **Language**: TypeScript\n    84→- **UI Framework**: React\n    85→- **AI Model**: Claude (Anthropic)\n    86→- **Protocol**: WebSocket + WebMCP\n    87→- **Build Tool**: Bun bundler\n    88→\n    89→## Usage Examples\n    90→\n    91→### Floating AI Chat (Recommended)\n    92→\n    93→The easiest way to add AI capabilities is using the built-in floating chat UI:\n    94→\n    95→```tsx\n    96→import { UseAIProvider } from '@use-ai/client';\n    97→import App from './App';\n    98→import { todoTools } from './tools';\n    99→\n   100→<UseAIProvider\n   101→  serverUrl=\"ws://localhost:8080\"\n   102→  showFloatingChat={true}\n   103→  globalTools={todoTools}\n   104→>\n   105→  <App />\n   106→</UseAIProvider>\n   107→```\n   108→\n   109→This displays a floating \"AI\" button in the bottom-right corner. Users can click it to open a chat interface and interact with your app using natural language.\n   110→\n   111→### Programmatic API\n   112→\n   113→For custom UI implementations:\n   114→\n   115→```tsx\n   116→import { UseAIProvider, useAI } from '@use-ai/client';\n   117→\n   118→function App() {\n   119→  const { response, loading, generate } = useAI({\n   120→    tools: {\n   121→      addTodo: {\n   122→        fn: (input) => addTodo(input.text),\n   123→        config: {\n   124→          description: 'Add a new todo item',\n   125→          parameters: 