            "content": "# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nA TypeScript monorepo for building AI-powered React applications with WebSocket-based AI agent integration. The library enables React components to expose tools (functions) to Claude AI, which can then call them via natural language prompts.\n\n## Development Commands\n\n### Setup\n```bash\nbun install                    # Install dependencies\n```\n\n### Development\n```bash\nexport ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...  # Required for server\nbun run start:server           # Start AI server (port 8080)\nbun run dev                    # Start example app with hot reload\n```\n\nThe server must be running before starting the example app. The example app runs at http://localhost:3000.\n\n### Building\n```bash\nbun run build                  # Build all packages (client, server, example)\nbun run build:client           # Build @use-ai/client only\nbun run build:server           # Build @use-ai/server only\n```\n\nBuild process for packages: Bun bundles code → TypeScript generates type declarations.\n\n### Testing\n```bash\nbun test                       # Run all tests\n```\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Monorepo Structure\n- `packages/client/` - `@use-ai/client`: React hooks library for AI integrations\n- `packages/server/` - `@use-ai/server`: WebSocket server for AI agent hosting\n- `apps/example/` - Example AI-powered todo list demonstrating the library\n\n### Core Data Flow\n\n1. **Tool Registration**: Client registers tools (defined with Zod schemas) via WebSocket to server\n2. **User Prompt**: User sends natural language prompt through UI\n3. **AI Processing**: Server forwards prompt + tool definitions to Claude API\n4. **Tool Execution**: Claude returns tool_use blocks → Server sends `tool_call` to client → Client executes tool locally → Client sends result back\n5. **Response**: Server sends tool results to Claude → Claude generates final response → Server streams to client\n\n### Key Architectural Patterns\n\n#### Client-Side Tool Execution\n- Tools are **defined and executed on the client** (where application state lives)\n- Server acts as **coordinator** between Claude API and client tools\n- This enables tools to access React state, browser APIs, and local data directly\n\n#### WebSocket Protocol\nAll messages follow `{ type: string, data: object }` format:\n\n**Client → Server:**\n- `register_tools`: Send tool definitions (JSON Schema format)\n- `prompt`: Send user prompt with optional conversation ID\n- `tool_response`: Return tool execution result for a specific tool call\n\n**Server → Client:**\n- `tool_call`: Request tool execution with `{ toolCallId, name, input }`\n- `response`: Final AI response with conversation ID\n- `error`: Error messages\n\n#### Promise-Based Tool Coordination\nThe server uses promises to synchronously wait for async tool execution across the WebSocket boundary:\n```typescript\n// Server creates promise and stores resolver\nconst promise = new Promise(resolve => {\n  session.pendingToolCalls.set(toolCallId, resolve);\n});\n// Send tool_call to client\nthis.sendMessage(ws, 'tool_call', { toolCallId, name, input });\n// Wait for client to execute and send tool_response\nconst result = await promise;\n```\n\n#### Conversation History Management\n- Server maintains **full conversation history per WebSocket session**\n- History includes user messages, assistant messages (with tool_use blocks), and tool results\n- Enables multi-turn conversations with context preservation\n- History is lost on disconnect (session-based, not persisted to database)\n\n#### Tool Aggregation Pattern\n- `UseAIProvider` maintains a registry of tools from all mounted `useAI` hooks\n- Tools from multiple components are merged into a single set\n- Each hook gets a unique ID for registration/cleanup\n- Enables compositional tool registration across component tree\n\n### Tool Definition System\n\nTools are defined using `defineTool()` with Zod schemas:\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineTool } from '@use-ai/client';\nimport { z } from 'zod';\n\nconst addTodo = defineTool(\n  'Add a new todo item to the list',\n  z.object({ text: z.string() }),\n  (input) => {\n    // Implementation with typed input\n    return { success: true, message: 'Todo added' };\n  }\n);\n```\n\n**Under the hood:**\n- Zod schema is converted to JSON Schema (via `zod-to-json-schema`) for Claude API\n- Original Zod schema is retained for runtime validation\n- `_execute()` method validates input with Zod before calling function\n- TypeScript types are inferred from Zod schema\n\n### State Synchronization Pattern\n\nThe example app demonstrates a pub/sub pattern for keeping UI in sync when tools mutate state:\n\n```typescript\nconst listeners = new Set<() => void>();\n\nexport function subscribeTodos(listener: () => void) {\n  listeners.add(listener);\n  return () => listeners.delete(listener);\n}\n\nfunction notifyListeners() {\n  listeners.forEach(fn => fn());\n}\n\n// Tools call notifyListeners() after state mutations\n```\n\nThis enables both AI operations and manual UI operations to update the same state.\n\n## TypeScript Configuration\n\n- **Strict mode enabled**: All type checks enforced\n- **Module system**: ESM throughout (`\"type\": \"module\"` in all package.json files)\n- **Module resolution**: `\"bundler\"` (Bun-specific)\n- **Target**: ES2022\n- Never use `any` type unless unavoidable\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Client Package\n- `zod` (v4.x): Schema validation and JSON Schema generation\n- `zod-to-json-schema`: Converts Zod schemas to JSON Schema for Claude API\n- `react` (peer dependency): ^18.0.0\n\n### Server Package\n- `@anthropic-ai/sdk`: Claude API integration\n- `ws`: WebSocket server implementation\n\n## Important Implementation Details\n\n### Connection Management\n- Client auto-reconnects on disconnect (5 attempts with exponential backoff)\n- Each `useAI` hook creates a dedicated WebSocket client instance\n- Provider monitors connection status for UI feedback\n\n### Error Handling\n- Tool execution errors are caught and sent back to Claude as `tool_result` content\n- Zod validation errors propagate as tool execution errors\n- Server errors sent as `error` messages to client\n- Client handles errors via optional `onError` callback in `useAI` hook\n\n### Build System\n- Bun is used for both runtime and bundling\n- Package builds: `bun build` creates bundle → `tsc --emitDeclarationOnly` generates types\n- Example app build: `bun build --target browser --minify`\n- All packages output ESM modules\n\n### Environment Variables\n- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`: Required for server to communicate with Claude API\n- Server runs on port 8080 (hardcoded in `packages/server/src/start.ts`)\n\n### File Naming Conventions\n- React components: PascalCase (e.g., `FloatingAIButton.tsx`)\n- Utilities and hooks: camelCase (e.g., `defineTool.ts`, `useAI.ts`)\n- Main entry points: `index.ts` or `index.tsx`\n",
